y symptomatic angiodysplasia may present as massive bleed\n[RAG context for 'Initially' (score=0.87):]\n  Source: Adults forms of scimitar syndrome. > Etiology\n  In anomalous venous connections, pulmonary veins connect abnormally to the systemic venous system. In anomalous venous drainage, the veins connect to the anatomically correct location, but due to an i\n[Indirect reasoning chains (clinical inference):]\n  worsening symptoms of previously diagnosed acute sinusitis after decongestant treatment → bacterial superinfection of a viral sinusitis → Bacterial Superinfection of Sinus\n    (frequency: frequent)\n    Suggestion: Evaluate for bacterial superinfection via nasal culture or increased inflammatory markers to confirm progression to Bacterial Superinfection of Sinus\n  nasal discharge with worsening pain after initial improvement → nasal mucosal abscess formation with secondary hemorrhage → Nasal Mucosal Abscess with Secondary Hemorrhage\n    (frequency: occasional)\n    Suggestion: Assess for focal nasal swelling, fever, or signs of local tissue necrosis to support nasal mucosal abscess as the intermediate mechanism\n  7-year-old male with asthma history and persistent sinus symptoms → foreign body-induced mechanical obstruction → Foreign Body / Mechanical Obstruction\n    (frequency: rare)\n    Suggestion: Perform nasal endoscopy to rule out retained foreign body as a cause of persistent symptoms\n\nWhen indirect_reasoning_chains are present, generate candidates that investigate the INTERMEDIATE phenotype to confirm or rule out the indirect association."}
